# Build context guard for the mediator image (01.3 SF-4).
#
# The mediator's build context is this solution root, not `images/`, because the
# image must carry two things that live outside `images/`: the resolved policy
# artifact (`policy/resolved/`, read from the image layer and never from a path an
# agent can write) and the mediator's configuration templates (`mediator/config/`,
# added by SF-5 and SF-6). A root context sends everything here to the daemon by
# default -- including `references/.env_keys` (live credentials) and
# `mediator/identity/ca/mediator-ca.key` (the CA private key that criterion 9 says
# never enters an image layer or the mediator).
#
# So this is deny-all plus an explicit allowlist. A new path the image needs must be
# added here deliberately; the failure mode is a build error, not a leaked secret.
#
# Note: `images/.dockerignore` governs the AGENT builds, whose context is `images/`.
# A .dockerignore applies to the context root it sits in, so both files are needed.
*

!images/mediator
!policy/resolved
!mediator/config
# One file, not the directory: stage 1 of the mediator's startup self-check (SF-7)
# calls the SAME schema validator the compiler uses, and the rest of scripts/ has no
# business in the enforcement point -- issue-identity.sh in particular is the offline
# CA tool whose whole premise is that it never runs here.
!scripts/compile-policy.sh

# Trailing denies. Docker's rules are order-sensitive -- the LAST matching line
# decides -- so these sit below every `!` above and re-exclude regardless of what
# an allowlist entry admitted. That is the whole point of their position: today
# the deny-all already covers them and these lines are redundant, but the moment
# someone adds `!mediator/**` or `!references/**` above, they are the difference
# between a redundant line and a leaked private key.
#
# They are not an absolute guard. A future `!` placed BELOW this block would
# re-admit the path silently. Add new allowlist entries above this comment, never
# under it.
**/.DS_Store
mediator/identity
mediator/identity/**
references
references/**
